    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0408" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1123 Seymour, Walter F./16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-04T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 4,
                                1928—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 12 noon.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>598. My 545, July 17, 7 p.m. Following telegram has been sent to Nationalist
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs [and] is reported for your information.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Again referring to my despatch of May 10 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >15</hi>?]<anchor n="51" xml:id="d245-f1"/> concerning the murder of Dr.
                        Seymour, and to that of your predecessor of May 19th<anchor n="52"
                            xml:id="d245-f2"/> stating that an investigation had been ordered, I
                        have the honor once more to request information as to what has been done
                        towards the apprehension and punishing of those responsible for this
                        crime.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d245-f1" n="51" xml:id="d245-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 377, May 21, from the Minister in China, <ref target="#pg286">p.
                        286</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d245-f2" n="52" xml:id="d245-f2-content">
                <p>See despatch of May 28 from the Chinese Commissioner of Foreign Affairs at
                    Shanghai to the American consul general, <ref target="#pg287">p. 287</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
